IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch7-p1`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch7-p6`

-- Tests for ssc9-sch7-p6.l4 (Schedule 7 Part VI). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- Schedule 7 Part VI`

§§ `Paragraph 14`

-- Reading (e): a death before 11 April 1988 is inside the scope the sentence states (the other reading answers NOTHING).
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 14(1) this Part has effect in relation to the death` (Date 10 4 1988) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 14(1) this Part has effect in relation to the death` (Date 11 4 1988) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 14(1A): the commencement day is an input. A claim after it -> FALSE; on or before -> NOTHING; unknown -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 14(1A) a claim for industrial death benefit may be made` (Date 2 1 2000) (JUST (Date 1 1 2000)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 14(1A) a claim for industrial death benefit may be made` (Date 1 1 2000) (JUST (Date 1 1 2000)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 14(1A) a claim for industrial death benefit may be made` (Date 31 12 1999) (JUST (Date 1 1 2000)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- 14(2): the deceased is the person whose death the benefit is claimed or payable for ("means": closed).
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 14(2) the person is the deceased` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 14(2) the person is the deceased` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 14(1A) a claim for industrial death benefit may be made` (Date 2 1 2000) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 15 -- widow`

-- Argument order: widow; residing with him; payments provided or procured by the deceased; receiving; entitled (court order etc.); would but for the accident
-- have been receiving; weekly amount; prescribed amount.
-- (a) residing with him: entitled.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) maintenance of 10 or more, provided by the deceased, being received: entitled; of 9.99: not; exactly the prescribed amount: yes.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 10 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 9.99 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Entitled to receive under an order she has taken reasonable steps to enforce; or would but for the relevant accident have been receiving.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 12 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 12 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Payments not provided or procured by the deceased do not count (15(4)(a)); not receiving or entitled -> no.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 12 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 12 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not the widow.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 12 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 15(2): argument order: entitled; death day; day she remarried; day she died; the day. Commencing from the death (a day before it: NOTHING, a stated start); until she remarries (that day and after: FALSE); for life (after the day she died: NOTHING, a stated period).
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 1 3 1985) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 28 2 1985) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST (Date 1 6 1990)) NOTHING (Date 31 5 1990) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST (Date 1 6 1990)) NOTHING (Date 1 6 1990) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 6 1995)) (Date 1 6 1995) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 6 1995)) (Date 2 6 1995) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 1 3 1986) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` NOTHING (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 1 3 1986) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(3) the pension may be payable for the period` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 15(3) the pension may be payable for the period` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 16 -- widow's rate`

-- 16(2)(b): over 50 at the death -> higher; else, if she had an allowance period, over 40 at its end -> higher; otherwise not by age.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` (JUST FALSE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 16: argument order: day; death day; initial; higher; lower (Schedule 4 amounts 50, 40, 30); child allowance; age answer; incapable; pregnant.
-- On the day of the death and through day 181: the initial rate. Day 182 on: the permanent rate.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1985) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 29 8 1985) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 30 8 1985) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 30
-- 1 Mar 1985 + 181 days = 29 Aug 1985 (Mar 30 left, Apr 30, May 31, Jun 30, Jul 31, Aug 29: 30+30+31+30+31 = 152 to 31 Jul; +29 = 181). Day 182 is 30 Aug.
-- Before the death: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 28 2 1985) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- After the initial period, each limb of 16(2) gives the higher rate: (a) child allowance; (b) age; (c) incapable; (d) pregnant.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1986) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1986) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1986) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1986) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 40
-- None of the limbs: the lower rate. Age unknown and no other limb: NOTHING. Age unknown but another limb holds: higher.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1986) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1986) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1986) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST 50) (JUST 40) (JUST 30) TRUE NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 40
-- The Schedule 4 table omitted: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` (Date 1 3 1986) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 17 -- widower`

#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(1) the widower is entitled to death benefit` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(1) the widower is entitled to death benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(1) the widower is entitled to death benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(1) the widower is entitled to death benefit` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 17(2): argument order: entitled; death day; day the widower died; Schedule 4 rate (25); the day.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) the weekly rate of the widower's pension on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING (JUST 25) (Date 1 3 1985) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) the weekly rate of the widower's pension on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING (JUST 25) (Date 28 2 1985) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) the weekly rate of the widower's pension on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST (Date 1 6 1990)) (JUST 25) (Date 1 6 1990) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) the weekly rate of the widower's pension on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) (JUST (Date 1 6 1990)) (JUST 25) (Date 2 6 1990) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) the weekly rate of the widower's pension on the day` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 1 3 1986) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) the weekly rate of the widower's pension on the day` (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING (JUST 25) (Date 1 3 1986) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) the weekly rate of the widower's pension on the day` NOTHING (Date 1 3 1985) NOTHING (JUST 25) (Date 1 3 1986) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 18 -- the deceased's family`

-- Argument order: deceased was entitled to child benefit; the person is the widow; widow entitled to death benefit (not a gratuity); the person entitled to child benefit; the person is prescribed.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` TRUE TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A prescribed person, not the widow, entitled to child benefit: NOTHING (subject to paragraph 19); a person neither widow nor prescribed: NOTHING (the text names two persons and does not say only); not entitled to child benefit for the period: FALSE; the deceased not entitled at his death: NOTHING (a "where").
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The weekly allowance: 2 children at the Schedule 4 amount of 9.5 -> 19; not entitled -> 0; unknown -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the weekly allowance` (JUST TRUE) 2 (JUST 9.5) EQUALS JUST 19
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the weekly allowance` (JUST FALSE) 2 (JUST 9.5) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the weekly allowance` NOTHING 2 (JUST 9.5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the weekly allowance` (JUST TRUE) 2 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 18(2) is Part I's paragraph 5(1): living with him -> NOTHING; neither -> FALSE.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(2) the allowance for the child may be payable` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(2) the allowance for the child may be payable` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 18(2) the allowance for the child may be payable` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 19 -- limits`

#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 19 the person is the one entitled to the allowance for the child` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 19 the person is the one entitled to the allowance for the child` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 19 the person is the one entitled to the allowance for the child` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 19 the person is the one entitled to the allowance for the child` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 20 -- constant attendance allowance`

-- Argument order: death day; entitled to a section 104 increase (a payment by way of increase of disablement pension); amount of the increase; Schedule 4 para 2(a) amount (say 20); would have been so entitled but for in-patient treatment.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE 20 (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE 19.99 (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 1 1 1980) FALSE 0 (JUST 20) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 1 1 1980) FALSE 0 (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE 25 NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Neither limb is met: the "If" fails whatever Schedule 4 says, so the missing Schedule 4 amount does not matter.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 1 1 1980) FALSE 0 NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 20(3): "does not affect death benefit" for a death before 26 July 1971 is a flat negative (FALSE); on 26 July 1971 the paragraph applies.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 25 7 1971) TRUE 25 (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 25 7 1971) TRUE 25 NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` (Date 26 7 1971) TRUE 25 (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `Paragraph 21 -- pulmonary disease`

-- Argument order: death day; died of a pulmonary disease; entitled to benefit for pneumoconiosis etc.; assessed extent; the hypothetical extent; regulations provide otherwise.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE TRUE (JUST 50) (JUST 60) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE TRUE (JUST 49.99) (JUST 60) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE TRUE (JUST 49) (JUST 49) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE TRUE (JUST 50) (JUST 50) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Requirement (b) fails on the assessed extent: the hypothetical extent is not needed.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE TRUE (JUST 49) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 21(2): the hypothetical extent under 50 makes (b) unsatisfied, unless regulations provide otherwise.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE TRUE (JUST 60) (JUST 49) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE TRUE (JUST 60) (JUST 49) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE TRUE (JUST 60) (JUST 50) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE TRUE (JUST 60) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST 60) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) FALSE TRUE (JUST 60) (JUST 60) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 1 1 1980) TRUE FALSE (JUST 60) (JUST 60) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 21(3): "does not affect death benefit" for a death before 30 March 1977 is a flat negative (FALSE); on the day itself the paragraph applies.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 29 3 1977) TRUE TRUE (JUST 60) (JUST 60) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 29 3 1977) TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` (Date 30 3 1977) TRUE TRUE (JUST 60) (JUST 60) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
